memory is module
memory purpose "Show a region-owned list that grows, is read, changed, iterated, and cleared"
memory path memory
memory imports standard.console
memory imports standard.math
memory imports standard.compare
memory imports standard.list
memory exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

showInt is operation
showInt purpose "Print one whole number on its own line"
showInt invariant none
showInt typeParameter none
showInt input value Int64 copied
showInt output none
showInt outputOwnedBy none
showInt raises none
showInt effect write console.stdout
showInt uses stdoutWriter
showInt memoryHeap false
showInt async false
showInt maxRecursion none
showInt label begin loopKind none
showInt label begin within none
showInt label done loopKind none
showInt label done within none
showInt let none
showInt at begin do writeValue
showInt at begin branch ifError writeValue goto done else goto done
showInt at done return ok none

writeValue is call
writeValue rationale "A test program has nowhere to report a failed write"
writeValue in showInt
writeValue invokes console.writeIntegerLine
writeValue argument value Int64 value copy
writeValue result none
writeValue ownedBy none
writeValue cleanedBy none
writeValue borrows none
writeValue catch writeError console.WriteError
writeValue suppresses console.WriteError.failed

Numbers is typeInstance
Numbers purpose "A growable list of whole numbers"
Numbers in none
Numbers instantiates list.List Int64

main is operation
main purpose "Run the case and print what it computes"
main invariant none
main typeParameter none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwnedBy none
main raises none
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memoryHeap true
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main label fill loopKind counted
main label fill within none
main label fill maxIterations 100
main label fill counter index
main label appendStep loopKind none
main label appendStep within fill
main label report loopKind none
main label report within none
main label showLastStep loopKind none
main label showLastStep within none
main label readBack loopKind none
main label readBack within none
main label showFirstStep loopKind none
main label showFirstStep within none
main label pastEnd loopKind none
main label pastEnd within none
main label showBad loopKind none
main label showBad within none
main label sumItems loopKind forEach
main label sumItems within none
main label sumItems maxIterations 100
main label sumItems over numbers
main label addItem loopKind none
main label addItem within sumItems
main label summed loopKind none
main label summed within none
main label broken loopKind none
main label broken within none
main let zero Int64 0 immutable
main let one Int64 1 immutable
main let hundred Int64 100 immutable
main let lastIndex Int64 99 immutable
main let fortyTwo Int64 42 immutable
main let index Int64 0 mutable
main let total Int64 0 mutable
main let failCode ExitCode 1 immutable
main let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable
main at begin do makeNumbers
main at begin goto fill
main at fill do filled
main at fill branch if isFilled goto report else goto appendStep
main at appendStep do appendIndex
main at appendStep do advance
main at appendStep set index nextIndex
main at appendStep goto fill
main at report do countNumbers
main at report do showCount
main at report do readLast
main at report branch ifError readLast goto broken else goto showLastStep
main at showLastStep do showLast
main at showLastStep do replaceFirst
main at showLastStep branch ifError replaceFirst goto broken else goto readBack
main at readBack do readFirst
main at readBack branch ifError readFirst goto broken else goto showFirstStep
main at showFirstStep do showFirst
main at showFirstStep do readPastEnd
main at showFirstStep branch ifError readPastEnd goto pastEnd else goto broken
main at pastEnd match pastEndError list.IndexOutOfRange
main at pastEnd case list.IndexOutOfRange.outOfRange bind badIndex Int64 goto showBad
main at showBad do printBad
main at showBad goto sumItems
main at sumItems branch ifNext numbers bind item Int64 goto addItem else goto summed
main at addItem do addToTotal
main at addItem set total newTotal
main at addItem goto sumItems
main at summed do showTotal
main at summed do emptyIt
main at summed do countAgain
main at summed do showEmpty
main at summed return ok okCode
main at broken return ok failCode

